      "side": 1,
      "message": "You need NET_CAPABILITY_INTERNET both here and in wifiNc2, because:\n\n03-18 08:52:26.357 13357 13389 E ConnectivityService: BUG: NetworkAgentInfo{network{64509}  handle{277067450994701}  ni{WIFI CONNECTED extra: } Score(60 ; KeepConnected : 0 ; Policies : EVER_VALIDATED_NOT_AVOIDED_WHEN_BAD\u0026IS_VALIDATED)  everValidated lastValidated  lp{{InterfaceName: test_wlan0 LinkAddresses: [ ] DnsAddresses: [ ] Domains: null MTU: 0 Routes: [ ]}}  nc{[ Transports: WIFI Capabilities: INTERNET\u0026NOT_RESTRICTED\u0026TRUSTED\u0026NOT_VPN\u0026VALIDATED\u0026NOT_ROAMING\u0026FOREGROUND\u0026NOT_SUSPENDED\u0026NOT_VCN_MANAGED TransportInfo: \u003cSSID: \u003cunknown ssid\u003e, BSSID: AA:AA:AA:AA:AA:AA, MAC: 02:00:00:00:00:00, Security type: -1, Supplicant state: UNINITIALIZED, Wi-Fi standard: 0, RSSI: -127, Link speed: -1Mbps, Tx Link speed: 0Mbps, Max Supported Tx Link speed: 0Mbps, Rx Link speed: 0Mbps, Max Supported Rx Link speed: 0Mbps, Frequency: -1MHz, Net ID: -1, Metered hint: false, score: 0, isUsable: true, CarrierMerged: false, SubscriptionId: -1, IsPrimary: 0\u003e UnderlyingNetworks: Null]}  factorySerialNumber\u003d-1} lost immutable capabilities:immutable capabilities changed: INTERNET|NOT_RESTRICTED|NOT_VPN -\u003e NOT_RESTRICTED|NOT_VPN\n\nThis is because because the TestNetworkAgentWrapper constructor that takes a NetworkCapabilities object (i.e., line 15595) adds NET_CAPABILITY_INTERNET to the passed-in capabilities, but the setNetworkCapabilities call at line 15608 does not.\n\nAs a result, this test it not really testing that the default network switches to cell due to validation - the default network is switching to cell because wifi lost the INTERNET capability.\n\nBecause this is really non-obvious (sorry!) you can prevent against this test breaking in the future by adding additional assertions:\n\n        // Wi-Fi is still connected and would become the default network if cell were to disconnect.\n        mCellNetworkAgent.disconnect();\n        mDefaultNetworkCallback.expectAvailableCallbacksUnvalidated(mWiFiNetworkAgent);\n\nWhen you do that, it turns out that the test fails, because the network is being torn down because wifiNc2 doesn\u0027t include NOT_VCN_MANAGED. Once you fix that, the test fails again because the BSSID update triggers a capability change. You can fix that with:\n\n        // TODO: register the callbacks with NETWORK_SETTINGS so we can check the unredacted BSSID\n        // in the WifiInfo.\n        mDefaultNetworkCallback.expectCapabilitiesThat(mWiFiNetworkAgent, (nc) -\u003e\n                !((WifiInfo) nc.getTransportInfo()).getBSSID().equals(\"AA:AA:AA:AA:AA:AA\")\n        );\n\nI managed to get the test to pass locally, which means the code is correct. So we we can probably leave this test as is and fix it in a follow-up. I have some code in my tree that works and I can upload a follow-up CL.",
